ounty","/arc-plc/kentucky/hardin-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and April to May came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them. In 2025 that same middle went to 69% of normal in July to August and 63% in November to December. So far in 2026 it read 46% in January to February and 154% in June to July. Every grid listed had its driest year in 1963, with grid 20876 at 58% that year.</p>"}
